            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Identify",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sweet pea (matar) or garden pea plants in a garden or a nearby field."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.442,
            0.773,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Select two juvenile (less developed) flower bud and three freshly blossomed flowers on the same pea plant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.785,
            0.418,
            0.854,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 8",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Curiosity "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 12",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.474,
            0.774,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Carefully remove the stamens from one of the two selected flowers buds and one of the three selected flowers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.506,
            0.774,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Take muslin cloth bags and loosely wrap them around the flower bud, the flower bud of which stamens are removed, the flower of which stamens are removed and a freshly blossomed flower (Fig. 11.12)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.555,
            0.774,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Leave one freshly blossomed flower uncovered (without muslin cloth bag)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.586,
            0.775,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Observe them regularly and notice the development of fruits in place of the flowers that were not covered with muslin cloth. Allow them to grow for a few more days."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.634,
            0.774,
            0.683
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Once the pods are fully developed in the flowers without muslin cloth, remove the muslin cloth from all the wrapped flowers and observe them."
            }
          ]
        },
